From: php-eol-patch project
Subject: [PATCH] Provide ZSTR_MAX_LEN for vanilla PHP 7.3

Vanilla PHP 7.3 does not define ZSTR_MAX_LEN (introduced in PHP 7.4).
The CVE-2026-109618/109619 minimal mitigation patch (0001) uses it in the
VM CONCAT integer-overflow checks, so without this compat shim the patched
tree does not compile. Same semantics as the PHP 7.4 definition.

--- a/Zend/zend_string.h
+++ b/Zend/zend_string.h
@@ -76,6 +76,13 @@
 
 #define _ZSTR_STRUCT_SIZE(len) (_ZSTR_HEADER_SIZE + len + 1)
 
+/* Added by php-eol-patch 0002: ZSTR_MAX_LEN does not exist in vanilla 7.3,
+   but the CVE-2026-109618/109619 mitigation patch uses it in the VM
+   CONCAT overflow checks. Same definition as PHP 7.4+ provides. */
+#ifndef ZSTR_MAX_LEN
+#define ZSTR_MAX_LEN (SIZE_MAX - _ZSTR_HEADER_SIZE - 1)
+#endif
+
 #define ZSTR_ALLOCA_ALLOC(str, _len, use_heap) do { \
 	(str) = (zend_string *)do_alloca(ZEND_MM_ALIGNED_SIZE_EX(_ZSTR_STRUCT_SIZE(_len), 8), (use_heap)); \
 	GC_SET_REFCOUNT(str, 1); \
